# Empty on purpose — this app has no static assets under public/; the favicon is generated
# via src/app/icon.tsx (next/og's ImageResponse), not a static file here (see CLAUDE.md's
# "Known gaps" — the favicon bullet). This placeholder exists only so git tracks the
# directory at all: git never tracks empty directories, so without this, a fresh clone (or
# CI checkout) simply has no public/ folder on disk — found failing in CI 2026-08-22 when
# frontend/Dockerfile's `COPY --from=builder /app/public ./public/` errored with
# "/app/public": not found, for exactly this reason.
